he Commissioner and made available for public inspection during normal business hours, and posted on the website of the Commissioner. Each summary shall also be available to the public, on request, by fax or mail. 24. (1) The summary shall : (a)subject to subsection (3), set out the source and nature, but not the value, of the income, assets and liabilities referred to in the Member’s statement filed under section 20;(b) identify any contracts or subcontracts referred to in paragraph 21(1)(c) and describe their subject-matter and nature;(c) list the names of any affiliated corporations referred to in that statement; (d) include a copy of any statements of disclosure filed by the Member under subsections 14(3), 15(1) and 21(3); (e) list the positions and corporations, trade or professional associations and trade unions disclosed under paragraph 21(1)(e); and (f) list any trusts disclosed under paragraph 21(1)(b.1). Rob Morrison · Member of Parliament Declaration type Disclosure Summaries (Code) Disclosure date January 20, 2026 Regime Conflict of Interest Code for Members of the House of Commons Description LiabilitiesTwo mortgages with CIBC, with spouse.Line of credit with CIBC.Investment in Private CorporationsControlling interest in Ram Strategic Security Consulting Ltd., a security consulting business located in Creston, British Columbia.Nominal interest in Archer Biotech Corp., a clean-tech energy supply business in Vancouver, British Columbia.Nominal interest in MOTB Global LLC, an investment company in Arizona, United States.ActivitiesDirector of Ram Strategic Security Consulting Ltd.Spouse's/Common-Law Partner's source(s) of incomeLast 12 months:Employment income from Dr. Lawrence Jewett.Next 12 months:Employment income from Dr. Lawrence Jewett. Disclosed on January 20, 2026","url":"https://www.ethicscanada.ca/en/public-registry/Details?declarationId=f490dce1-71d0-f011-819f-001dd8b72449"}],"other":[]},"lobbying":{"total":109,"first":"2020-02-04","last":"2026-1